This method removes all occurrences of a given value (val) from the array in-place and returns the new length of the array after removal.

It uses a pointer pos to track the position where the next valid (non-val) element should be placed.
It loops through the array:

If the current element is not equal to val, it copies it to pos and increments pos.


After the loop, the first pos elements of the array contain all valid elements.


Time Complexity:

O(n) → You traverse the array once.

Space Complexity:

O(1) → No extra space is used 

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
class Solution {
    public int removeElement(int[] nums, int val) {
       int pos=0;
       for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
        if(nums[i]!=val){
            nums[pos]=nums[i];
            pos++;
        }
       }
       return pos;
    }
}
